2026-09-27T10:32:16.1540769Z Description:
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1541260Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1541717Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1542847Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1544139Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1544271Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1544561Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1544961Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1545400Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1545536Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1545839Z ================
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1546021Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1546258Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1546812Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1547121Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1547290Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1547698Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1547939Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1548127Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1548676Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1549387Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1550468Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1551313Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1551480Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1552189Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1553082Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1553536Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1554042Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1554712Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1554859Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1555161Z ========
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1555340Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1557485Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1560026Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1560387Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1561178Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1643787Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1644834Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1645760Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1646420Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1647019Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1647206Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1647569Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1647775Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1649549Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1651322Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1652284Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1653589Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:32:16.1653902Z 
